{"name":"Pale Verdigris","hex":"#6f9892","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pale","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Light in color.","Having a pallor (a light color, especially due to sickness, shock, fright etc.)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To turn pale; to lose colour.","To become insignificant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pale"},{"term":"verdigris","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A blue-green patina or rust that forms on copper-containing metals.","Copper acetate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or coat with verdigris."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/verdigris"}],"entries":[{"title":"Verdigris","blocks":[{"text":"Verdigris is a common name for any of a variety of somewhat toxic copper salts of acetic acid, which range in colour from green to a bluish-green depending on their chemical composition. Once used as a medicine and pharmaceutical preparation, verdigris occurs naturally, creating a patina on copper, bronze, and brass, and is the main component of a historic green pigment used for artistic purposes from antiquity until the late 20th century, including in easel painting, polychromatic sculptures, and illumination of maps. However, due to its instability, its popularity declined as other green pigments became readily available. The instability of its appearance stems from its hydration level and basicity, which change as the pigment interacts with other materials over time."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verdigris","wikidata":"Q2351119"},{"title":"Colorfulness","blocks":[{"text":"Colorfulness, chroma and saturation are attributes of perceived color relating to chromatic intensity. As defined formally by the International Commission on Illumination (CIE) they respectively describe three different aspects of chromatic intensity, but the terms are often used loosely and interchangeably in contexts where these aspects are not clearly distinguished. The precise meanings of the terms vary by what other functions they are dependent on."},{"items":["Colorfulness is the \"attribute of a visual perception according to which the perceived color of an area appears to be more or less chromatic \". The colorfulness evoked by an object depends not only on its spectral reflectance but also on the strength of the illumination, and increases with the latter unless the brightness is very high.","Chroma is the \"colorfulness of an area judged as a proportion of the brightness of a similarly illuminated area that appears white or highly transmitting\". As a result, chroma is mostly only dependent on the spectral properties, and as such is seen to describe the object color. It is how different from a grey of the same lightness such an object color appears to be.","Saturation is the \"colorfulness of an area judged in proportion to its brightness\", which in effect is the perceived freedom from whitishness of the light coming from the area. An object with a given spectral reflectance exhibits approximately constant saturation for all levels of illumination, unless the brightness is very high."]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Brightness_and_colorfulness.png/330px-Brightness_and_colorfulness.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colorfulness","wikidata":"Q27673"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Verdigris.JPG/500px-Verdigris.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Verdigris.JPG/1280px-Verdigris.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Verdigris.JPG/500px-Verdigris.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Naturally occurring verdigris on exposed metal in the Prague Metro.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVerdigris.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Last_Supper_%28by_Giotto_di_Bondone%29_-_Capella_degli_Scrovegni_%28Padova%29.jpg/250px-Last_Supper_%28by_Giotto_di_Bondone%29_-_Capella_degli_Scrovegni_%28Padova%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Last_Supper_%28by_Giotto_di_Bondone%29_-_Capella_degli_Scrovegni_%28Padova%29.jpg/500px-Last_Supper_%28by_Giotto_di_Bondone%29_-_Capella_degli_Scrovegni_%28Padova%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Last_Supper_%28by_Giotto_di_Bondone%29_-_Capella_degli_Scrovegni_%28Padova%29.jpg/250px-Last_Supper_%28by_Giotto_di_Bondone%29_-_Capella_degli_Scrovegni_%28Padova%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALast_Supper_(by_Giotto_di_Bondone)_-_Capella_degli_Scrovegni_(Padova).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/CrocefissioneRaffaello.jpg/120px-CrocefissioneRaffaello.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/CrocefissioneRaffaello.jpg/250px-CrocefissioneRaffaello.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/CrocefissioneRaffaello.jpg/120px-CrocefissioneRaffaello.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrocefissioneRaffaello.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Sandro_botticelli%2C_nativit%C3%A0_mistica%2C_1500%2C_02_angeli.jpg/250px-Sandro_botticelli%2C_nativit%C3%A0_mistica%